# Project Structure (Expert Modular Reference)

> **This project uses a modular, feature-first architecture for maximum maintainability, scalability, and clarity.**  
> _For the authoritative structure and rationale, see [PROJECT_BLUEPRINT.md](PROJECT_BLUEPRINT.md)._

> **Expert Note:**
> If you add or update any app data JSON files (in `data/`) or project task files (e.g., `tasks.json`) in the future, you must document them in this structure and update this guide and the project blueprint accordingly. This ensures ongoing clarity, maintainability, and onboarding quality for all contributors.

```
Nutri Track app/
├── app/                # Next.js app directory (feature modules, API routes, layout)
│   ├── analytics/      # Analytics dashboard (feature module)
│   ├── dashboard/      # Main dashboard (feature module)
│   ├── exercise/       # Exercise tracking (feature module)
│   ├── food-logger/    # Food logging (feature module)
│   ├── meal-plan/      # Meal planning (feature module)
│   ├── performance/    # Performance analytics (feature module)
│   ├── water-tracker/  # Water intake tracking (feature module)
│   ├── layout.tsx      # App-wide layout
│   └── page.tsx        # App entry point
├── components/         # Shared, cross-feature React components (Button, Card, Header, etc.)
├── hooks/              # Custom React hooks (useAuth, useAnalytics, etc.)
├── lib/                # Core utilities, Prisma, validation schemas, helpers
├── services/           # Business logic, analytics, recommendations, monitoring
├── styles/             # Tailwind config, CSS Modules, global styles
│   ├── base/           # Reset, accessibility, critical CSS
│   ├── components/     # Component-level styles
│   ├── layout/         # Grid, layout utilities
│   └── utils/          # Animations, utility classes
├── types/              # TypeScript type definitions (deduplicated, domain-organized)
├── utils/              # General-purpose helpers, logging, audit, backup
├── prisma/             # Database schema and migrations
├── public/             # Static assets (images, icons, manifest)
├── providers/          # React context providers (global state, error boundaries, etc.)
├── scripts/            # Automation, migration, and utility scripts
├── config/             # Environment and security configs
├── docs/               # Documentation, audit reports, guides
├── data/               # App data JSON files (UIFix.json, ping.json, error_tracking.json, errorfree.json)
├── tasks/              # Taskmaster AI project management files
├── tests/              # All integration and unit tests
├── translations/       # i18n JSON files (user-facing text)
├── README.md           # Main documentation
├── API.md              # API documentation
├── PROJECT_BLUEPRINT.md# Architecture & onboarding reference
├── tasks.json          # Unified project tasks (shell + Task Master AI)
└── ...
```

#### Key Principles (from PROJECT_BLUEPRINT.md)
- **Strict modularity:** Each feature is self-contained in its own folder under `app/`.
- **Shared code only in** `components/`, `hooks/`, `services/`, `utils/`, and `types/`.
- **No feature-specific code in shared folders.**
- **TypeScript everywhere.**
- **All user-facing text in** `translations/`.
- **No legacy HTML, fix, or temp files** in the root or feature folders.
- **Accessibility and responsiveness** are first-class requirements.

#### Import Path Conventions
- **Feature code:** Use relative imports within the feature, absolute imports for shared code (e.g., `import { Button } from 'components/Button'`).
- **Shared code:** Never import feature-specific code.
- **Types:** Always import from `types/` or `lib/validations/`.
- **Update all imports** when moving or renaming files.

#### For More Details
- See [PROJECT_BLUEPRINT.md](PROJECT_BLUEPRINT.md) for rationale, onboarding, and architectural decisions.
- See the “Modular Architecture & Folder Structure” and “Key Files & Their Roles” sections for further guidance.

